,"2018-19":151074.0,"2019-20":156444.0,"2020-21":150152.0,"2021-22":154648.0,"2022-23":173767.0,"2023-24":184127.0,"2024-25":201106.0},"prov":{"description":"NET current expenditure - NET REVENUE EXPENDITURE (TOTAL OF LINES 800 TO 804)","form":"RS","row":"805","col":"1"}}]}],"context":[{"label":"Resident population","value":211439,"year":"2020 est.","kind":"int"},{"label":"GVA (balanced, total)","value":5845000.0,"year":"2023","kind":"money"},{"label":"GVA per head","value":28002,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"GDP per head","value":31148,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D council tax (area bill)","value":2420.15,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D \u2014 council's own element","value":2034.19,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"}]}},"dossier":{"summary":{"summary":"Calderdale ended 2025/26 with just \u00a32.68m of external investments \u2014 a single NatWest call account, down from \u00a36.2m a year earlier \u2014 against \u00a3137.6m of PWLB debt: the cash cushion is essentially gone. The report is unusually candid about why: years of SEND (schools funding) deficits and reserve drawdowns have worsened cashflow, forcing rolling short-term borrowing from other councils (\u00a3305k of interest in the year) even as \u00a39.98m of PWLB debt matured without replacement. Treasury costs overran budget by \u00a3654k because investment income fell \u00a31.54m short of plan. Internal borrowing will need replacing with new long-term PWLB loans in 2026/27, so a step-up in external debt is coming against a CFR of \u00a3237.3m.","fy":"2025/26","as_of_doc":"Annual Report on Treasury Management 2025/26","as_of_url":"https://calderdale.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s19943/8. Annual Treasury Management Report 2025-26 Audit Committee 27 July 2026 v2.pdf","as_of_date":"2026-07-27","signals":[{"code":"low-liquidity","headline":"External investments of \u00a32.68m at 31 March 2026 (one NatWest call account; \u00a36.2m a year earlier) against \u00a3137.6m of PWLB debt","why":"With almost no invested cash, day-to-day spending depends on continuously rolling short-term loans from other councils."},{"code":"dsg-deficit","headline":"The SEND funding deficit 'accumulated over a number of years continued to significantly impact on the Council's cashflow throughout' 2025/26, driving increased short-term borrowing","why":"A schools deficit parked behind the statutory accounting override is being financed with real borrowed cash today."},{"code":"reserves-drawdown","headline":"'Significant levels of Council reserves have been used' in recent years to fund additional costs and the increased SEND deficit, reducing balances and forcing short-term borrowing","why":"The cash that once backed reserves is spent, so internal borrowing capacity is exhausted and new pressure lands directly on external debt."}],"key_figures":[{"name":"cfr","value":"\u00a3237.3m (2024/25: \u00a3238.8m)","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":3},{"name":"borrowing","value":"\u00a3137,637,583 PWLB long-term debt, \u00a39.978m lower than a year earlier through maturities; no new PWLB borrowing taken in 2025/26","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":2},{"name":"investments","value":"\u00a32.68m external investments (down from \u00a36.2m at 31 March 2025)","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":4},{"name":"investments detail","value":"single NatWest investment call account, on call, average rate 1.75%","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":7},{"name":"treasury outturn vs budget","value":"overall cost \u00a310.831m vs \u00a310.177m budget \u2014 \u00a3654k overspend","as_at":"2025/26","page":5},{"name":"investment income vs budget","value":"interest earned \u00a3966k vs \u00a32.12m budget (\u00a31.54m short) as the cash position worsened","as_at":"2025/26","page":6},{"name":"short term borrowing cost","value":"\u00a3305,033 interest paid on short-term borrowing in the year","as_at":"2025/26","page":2},{"name":"interest paid long term","value":"\u00a35,085,508 interest paid on long-term PWLB debt; matured debt averaged 4.09%, remaining book 3.27%","as_at":"2025/26","page":2},{"name":"ccla property fund","value":"\u00a35m invested Nov 2019, valued \u00a34,339,437 (\u00a3661k below cost, +\u00a366,923 in year); \u00a3199,458 dividend in 2025/26","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":4},{"name":"limits","value":"operational boundary \u00a3210m and authorised limit \u00a3217m \u2014 remained within both","as_at":"2025/26","page":3}],"commercial":null,"tms_components":null},"compliance":null,"documents":[{"title":"5. Unaudited Statement of Accounts 2025-26","url":"https://Calderdale.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s19939/5-unaudited-statement-of-accounts-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Audit Committee","date":"27/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"8. Annual Treasury Management Report 2025-26 Audit Committee 27 July 2026 v2","url":"https://Calderdale.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s19943/8-annual-treasury-management-report-2025-26-audit-committee.pdf","committee":"Audit Committee","date":"27/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"6. Draft Annual Governance Statement 2025-26","url":"https://Calderdale.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s19940/6-draft-annual-governance-statement-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Audit Committee","date":"27/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"6. DRAFT ANNUAL GOVERNANCE STATEMENT 2025-26","url":"https://Calderdale.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s19941/6-draft-annual-governance-statement-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Audit Committee","date":"27/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"item 8 - Final Accounts 2025-26 - Revenue and Capital Outturn Position","url":"https://Calderdale.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s19852/item-8-final-accounts-2025-26-revenue-and-capital-outturn-po.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"13/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"2026 02 23 - Budget Council","url":"https://Calderdale.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s18817/2026-02-23-budget-council.pdf","committee":"Council","date":"19/03/2026","key":true},{"title":"Item 6a - Scrutiny Review \u2013 Revenue and Debt Collection by Calderdale Counci","url":"https://Ca